   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the elder law, in relation to requiring the commissioner of\nhealth to produce a report on the utilization and activity of the elderly\npharmaceutical insurance coverage program",
    "basePrintNo": "S7671",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7671-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §255, Eld L",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": ":us on;BILL NUMBER: S7671\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the elder law, in relation to requiring the commissioner\nof health to produce a report on the utilization and activity of the\nelderly pharmaceutical insurance coverage program\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to review the effectiveness of the EPIC\nprogram and identify any trends in utilization.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would require the department of health to\nproduce a report on the utilization and activity of the elderly pharma-\nceutical insurance coverage (EPIC) program. The report would include\nstatistical information on the program from 2022 to 2026, such as the\nnumber of persons enrolled, the number of enrollees that qualify through\nthe medicare savings program, and the number of participating provider\npharmacies. The report would also provide an evaluation of cost contain-\nment and outreach initiatives and would include enrollment and cost\nprojections for the 2027-2028 program years. This would be delivered to\nthe governor and the legislature by January 31, 2027.\n\nSection two would establish the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nN/A\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe EPIC program helps more than 325,000 income-eligible seniors aged 65\nand older receive affordable prescription medication in New York State.\nHowever, in the past few years, there have been numerous changes to\nEPIC. This report will assist in identifying trends in utilization and\nencourage analyses of the data compiled in the report.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
